This product is derived from "Phone Whisper" by Pol Alvarez
(https://github.com/kafkasl/phone-whisper), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
Changes include: removal of cloud transcription and cleanup, a redesigned interface, a larger on-device model
catalogue with install/uninstall, voice-activity detection, offline text cleanup, history, language selection,
trigger modes, and reliability work on the floating bubble.

Third-party components (full licence texts: app/src/main/assets/licenses/, shown in the app under
Settings > About > Open-source licences):
- sherpa-onnx (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx), Apache-2.0: Kotlin API sources in
  app/src/main/kotlin/com/k2fsa/sherpa/onnx, and the native library built by tools/build-native-libs.sh from the
  v1.12.28 sources with text-to-speech disabled (so it contains no espeak-ng / GPL code).
- Native components built into that library: kaldi-native-fbank, kaldi-decoder, kaldifst, OpenFst,
  simple-sentencepiece (Apache-2.0); nlohmann/json (MIT); KISS FFT and WebSocket++ (BSD-3-Clause);
  Eigen (MPL-2.0); Asio (Boost Software License 1.0).
- ONNX Runtime (https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime), MIT, and its bundled third-party notices.
- Silero VAD (https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad), MIT: app/src/main/assets/silero_vad.onnx.
- Java/Kotlin libraries, all Apache-2.0: AndroidX, Material Components, OkHttp/Okio, Kotlin and kotlinx.coroutines,
  Apache Commons (Compress, Codec, IO, Lang3), Guava ListenableFuture, Error Prone annotations.

Speech models are downloaded by the user at runtime and are not part of this repository. Each model has its own
licence; check it before redistributing a model.

The app icon was generated with an AI image model and processed locally.
